# IDE
.vs/
.idea/
*.suo

# The repository root .gitignore has `[Ll]ogs/` - a stock Visual Studio rule
# meant for log OUTPUT directories. It also matches two source folders here:
# src/Initiator.Domain/Logs/ and src/Initiator.Web/Views/Logs/. Without this
# exclusion git drops them from every commit without saying so, and the project
# builds on the machine that wrote it and fails in the container with "the
# namespace Logs does not exist".
#
# Renaming is not an option for the view folder: ASP.NET MVC resolves
# LogsController's views from Views/Logs/ by convention. So the exclusion is
# lifted, scoped to the source tree - real log output would never live under
# src/.
!src/**/Logs/
!src/**/Logs/**
